> Which model should I use as a base to the config model of the second-order latent? Weak, strong, strict, full?

Again, don't rely on the group.equal= argument.  That will only be useful in simple cases.  You need to use parameter labels in the syntax to add constraints manually, so you know exactly what model you are fitting at each step.

After you establish (at least partial) measurement invariance of first-order factors in a regular CFA, then you use the last model as the starting point for the next step, when you specify second-order factors.  Constraints on lower-order measurement parameters stay in place when you start the steps over again for second-order factors (i.e., the second-order "configural model" will have (at least partially) invariant first-order loadings, etc.).

