> My syntax is fine when I don't put last two sentences "tt=~ ch+ci+si
>
>                                                                                       tt ~~ 1*tt"
>
>
> How can I fix it?

Try only constraining either the factor variance or the first factor loading, not both.  Note that cfa() fixes the first factor loading to 1 by default, unless you tell it to fix factor variances instead using std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE.  Whatever is in your syntax will override what you tell the std.lv <http://std.lv>= argument, so you could free the loading using:

tt =~ NA*ch + ci + si
tt ~~ 1*tt

