Yvonne

Having negative factor scores is not unexpected, the factor scores are in the metric of the latent variable, not the items. If you use std.lv <http://std.lv>=T, the latent variable will be in a standardize metric with mean =0 and  sd=1, which will have people with negative numbers. If you use fix loading (the default) the latent variable will be in function of the 1 variable loading that is fix to 1, subjects with low scores in function of that variable will have negative numbers, and depending of which variable is chosen this will change

If you want to have the have the latent variable with the same metric as your items you need to use effects coding as your method of identification.

bye

